# Part 6: Azure App Service vs Azure Container Apps

Ab dono concepts ko compare karte hain.

## 12. Architecture Comparison

### Azure App Service

```text
             App Service Plan
                    |
       ┌────────────┼────────────┐
       |            |            |
       v            v            v
   Product       Order         User
   Web App       Web App       Web App
       |            |            |
       v            v            v
   .NET API      .NET API      .NET API
```

Teeno applications same App Service Plan ki compute capacity share kar sakti hain.

### Azure Container Apps

```text
          Container Apps Environment
                       |
          ┌────────────┼────────────┐
          |            |            |
          v            v            v
     Product App   Order App    User App
          |            |            |
          v            v            v
       Replicas     Replicas     Replicas
```

Har Container App ki independent replica scaling configuration ho sakti hai.

## 13. Main Differences

| Feature | Azure App Service | Azure Container Apps |
|---|---|---|
| Main Purpose | Web application hosting | Container application hosting |
| Deployment | .NET Code or Docker Image | Docker/OCI Image |
| Multiple APIs | Multiple Web Apps | Multiple Container Apps |
| Hosting Structure | App Service Plan → Web Apps | Environment → Container Apps |
| Scaling | Plan-level compute scaling; supported tiers par per-app scaling options | Independent replica scaling |
| Scale to Zero | Standard scale-to-zero model nahi hai | Supported |
| Revisions | Deployment Slots | Revisions |
| Traffic Splitting | Deployment Slots ke through supported workflows | Revision traffic splitting |
| Event-driven Scaling | Main strength nahi hai | KEDA-based event-driven scaling |
| Kubernetes Management | No | No, Kubernetes infrastructure Azure manage karta hai |

